// Weather the Storm ({1}{G} Instant): "You gain 3 life. Storm (When you cast
// this spell, copy it for each spell cast before it this turn.)" The simplest
// self-copying storm card — no targets — graduated as the corpus fixture for
// the Storm keyword ([CR#702.40a]) and its `Before(This)` cast-order count.
// The `Keyword(Storm)` macro carries the composite triggered ability; the
// printed line renders as the bare keyword name "Storm".
// waiver: keyword-line ordering seam — the renderer emits the keyword line
// FIRST (correct for a permanent's top-of-box keyword line, e.g. "Flying"),
// but on an instant/sorcery a spell keyword like storm prints AFTER the
// effect ("You gain 3 life." then "Storm"). Pure line-order divergence, no
// semantic difference; the keyword-on-a-spell placement is an unrelated
// renderer concern.
Normal(
  name: "Weather the Storm",
  mana_cost: [
    Generic(1),
    Green,
  ],
  types: [
    Instant,
  ],
  abilities: [
    Spell(effect: GainLife(3)),
    Keyword(Storm),
  ],
)
